1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:05,347
From 1857 to 1947, it took India ninety years to

2
00:00:05,347 --> 00:00:10,394
win its freedom from the most powerful empire on

3
00:00:10,394 --> 00:00:11,116
Earth.

4
00:00:11,866 --> 00:00:15,155
Hundreds of languages, many faiths, one dream.

5
00:00:15,155 --> 00:00:18,724
This is India's long road to independence, Chapter

6
00:00:18,724 --> 00:00:19,844
2, made simple.

7
00:00:22,494 --> 00:00:26,979
After the Great Uprising of 1857, Queen Victoria's

8
00:00:26,979 --> 00:00:31,287
Crown took direct control of India from the East

9
00:00:31,287 --> 00:00:32,606
India Company.

10
00:00:33,356 --> 00:00:36,614
The Royal Proclamation promised to respect Indian

11
00:00:36,614 --> 00:00:40,133
princes, to care for Indians like all other subjects,

12
00:00:40,133 --> 00:00:42,219
and not to impose Christianity.

13
00:00:42,219 --> 00:00:45,281
In practice, none of these promises were kept.

14
00:00:46,031 --> 00:00:49,362
Heavy land taxes caused terrible famines.

15
00:00:49,362 --> 00:00:53,247
The Arms Act of 1878 banned Indians from keeping

16
00:00:53,247 --> 00:00:58,243
weapons, and the Vernacular Press Act censored Indian-language

17
00:00:58,243 --> 00:00:59,194
newspapers.

18
00:00:59,944 --> 00:01:04,402
Meanwhile, reformers changed society from within.

19
00:01:04,402 --> 00:01:09,127
Raja Ram Mohan Roy founded the Brahmo Samaj in 1828,

20
00:01:09,127 --> 00:01:13,852
and Swami Dayananda Saraswati founded the Arya Samaj

21
00:01:13,852 --> 00:01:14,654
in 1875.

22
00:01:14,654 --> 00:01:19,379
Both fought child marriage and caste discrimination.

23
00:01:20,129 --> 00:01:23,461
Swami Vivekananda gave Indians courage with his

24
00:01:23,461 --> 00:01:24,364
famous call.

25
00:01:24,364 --> 00:01:28,043
Arise, awake, and stop not till the goal is reached.

26
00:01:28,793 --> 00:01:33,182
In 1875, Bankim Chandra Chattopadhyay composed Vande

27
00:01:33,182 --> 00:01:33,927
Mataram.

28
00:01:33,927 --> 00:01:35,997
I bow to the Motherland.

29
00:01:35,997 --> 00:01:40,633
It would become the battle cry of the freedom struggle.

30
00:01:41,383 --> 00:01:45,274
In 1885, the Indian National Congress held its first

31
00:01:45,274 --> 00:01:48,724
session in Bombay, with seventy-two delegates.

32
00:01:48,724 --> 00:01:52,321
Its early leaders, the Moderates, politely asked

33
00:01:52,321 --> 00:01:53,276
for reforms.

34
00:01:53,276 --> 00:01:55,698
The British mostly ignored them.

35
00:01:58,348 --> 00:01:59,715
Anger kept growing.

36
00:01:59,715 --> 00:02:02,789
The Kukas of Punjab boycotted foreign goods.

37
00:02:02,789 --> 00:02:06,137
Bal Gangadhar Tilak, called Lokmanya, roused the

38
00:02:06,137 --> 00:02:08,666
people through his newspaper Kesari.

39
00:02:08,666 --> 00:02:12,150
And Birsa Munda led the great tribal uprising, the

40
00:02:12,150 --> 00:02:12,834
Ulgulaan.

41
00:02:13,584 --> 00:02:17,329
In 1905, Viceroy Curzon split Bengal into two.

42
00:02:17,329 --> 00:02:20,197
The official reason was efficiency.

43
00:02:20,197 --> 00:02:21,552
The real reason?

44
00:02:21,552 --> 00:02:22,906
Divide and rule.

45
00:02:23,656 --> 00:02:24,557
It backfired.

46
00:02:24,557 --> 00:02:27,645
People burned foreign cloth, bought Indian-made

47
00:02:27,645 --> 00:02:30,798
goods, and tied rakhis on each other's wrists as

48
00:02:30,798 --> 00:02:32,857
a symbol of Hindu Muslim unity.

49
00:02:32,857 --> 00:02:35,688
This was the Swadeshi and Boycott movement.

50
00:02:36,438 --> 00:02:40,205
In 1906, the Congress adopted four goals: Swaraj,

51
00:02:40,205 --> 00:02:43,445
Swadeshi, Boycott, and National Education.

52
00:02:43,445 --> 00:02:47,589
The same year, the All-India Muslim League was founded

53
00:02:47,589 --> 00:02:48,342
in Dhaka.

54
00:02:49,092 --> 00:02:52,644
In 1907, at Surat, the Congress split in two.

55
00:02:52,644 --> 00:02:55,501
The Moderates wanted gradual reform.

56
00:02:55,501 --> 00:02:59,439
The Nationalists, Lal, Bal and Pal, wanted Swaraj.

57
00:03:00,189 --> 00:03:01,853
Some chose revolution.

58
00:03:01,853 --> 00:03:05,616
In 1908, eighteen-year-old Khudiram Bose was hanged

59
00:03:05,616 --> 00:03:06,991
for a bomb attack.

60
00:03:06,991 --> 00:03:10,609
Aurobindo Ghose faced the Alipore Bomb Trial, and

61
00:03:10,609 --> 00:03:12,925
Tilak was jailed for six years.

62
00:03:13,675 --> 00:03:15,292
The protests worked.

63
00:03:15,292 --> 00:03:18,987
In 1911, the partition of Bengal was cancelled,

64
00:03:18,987 --> 00:03:22,528
and the capital moved from Calcutta to Delhi.

65
00:03:23,278 --> 00:03:26,918
During World War One, the Ghadar Party tried to

66
00:03:26,918 --> 00:03:30,786
spark a mutiny in the army, and the fearless Bagha

67
00:03:30,786 --> 00:03:32,985
Jatin died fighting in 1915.

68
00:03:35,635 --> 00:03:39,590
In 1915, Mohandas Karamchand Gandhi returned from

69
00:03:39,590 --> 00:03:43,386
South Africa with a new weapon: satyagraha, the

70
00:03:43,386 --> 00:03:45,918
force of truth and nonviolence.

71
00:03:46,668 --> 00:03:50,059
In 1916, Tilak and Annie Besant launched the Home

72
00:03:50,059 --> 00:03:53,316
Rule Movement, and the Lucknow Pact brought the

73
00:03:53,316 --> 00:03:56,097
Congress and the Muslim League together.

74
00:03:56,847 --> 00:03:58,034
Then came 1919.

75
00:03:58,034 --> 00:04:01,448
The Rowlatt Act allowed arrest without trial.

76
00:04:01,448 --> 00:04:05,011
On the thirteenth of April, at Jallianwala Bagh

77
00:04:05,011 --> 00:04:09,019
in Amritsar, General Dyer blocked the exit and opened

78
00:04:09,019 --> 00:04:10,948
fire on an unarmed crowd.

79
00:04:11,698 --> 00:04:15,073
One thousand six hundred and fifty rounds, in about

80
00:04:15,073 --> 00:04:15,917
ten minutes.

81
00:04:15,917 --> 00:04:19,292
Over a thousand people killed, by Indian estimates.

82
00:04:19,292 --> 00:04:22,408
The whole nation was united in grief and anger.

83
00:04:23,158 --> 00:04:27,239
In 1920, Gandhi launched the Non-Cooperation Movement,

84
00:04:27,239 --> 00:04:29,689
joined by the Khilafat Movement.

85
00:04:29,689 --> 00:04:33,696
Indians boycotted British schools, courts, and cloth.

86
00:04:34,446 --> 00:04:38,457
But in 1922, protesters at Chauri Chaura set a police

87
00:04:38,457 --> 00:04:39,719
station on fire.

88
00:04:39,719 --> 00:04:42,096
Gandhi called off the movement.

89
00:04:42,096 --> 00:04:44,323
He would not accept violence.

90
00:04:46,973 --> 00:04:50,730
In 1928, the Simon Commission arrived without a

91
00:04:50,730 --> 00:04:52,452
single Indian member.

92
00:04:52,452 --> 00:04:54,956
Simon, go back, people shouted.

93
00:04:54,956 --> 00:04:58,870
Lala Lajpat Rai was beaten in a lathi charge, and

94
00:04:58,870 --> 00:05:00,200
died soon after.

95
00:05:00,950 --> 00:05:05,408
In December 1929, at the Lahore session, the Congress

96
00:05:05,408 --> 00:05:09,206
demanded Purna Swaraj, complete independence.

97
00:05:09,956 --> 00:05:13,295
In 1930, Gandhi walked three hundred and eighty

98
00:05:13,295 --> 00:05:16,773
kilometres to Dandi, and made salt from seawater,

99
00:05:16,773 --> 00:05:18,442
breaking an unjust law.

100
00:05:18,442 --> 00:05:21,433
The Civil Disobedience Movement had begun.

101
00:05:22,183 --> 00:05:25,851
Young revolutionaries Bhagat Singh, Sukhdev and

102
00:05:25,851 --> 00:05:28,296
Rajguru chose a different path.

103
00:05:28,296 --> 00:05:31,964
In 1931 they were hanged, and became heroes for

104
00:05:31,964 --> 00:05:32,957
generations.

105
00:05:33,707 --> 00:05:37,538
The Gandhi Irwin Pact of 1931 opened talks.

106
00:05:37,538 --> 00:05:41,805
The Poona Pact of 1932 settled a dispute between

107
00:05:41,805 --> 00:05:43,634
Gandhi and Doctor B.

108
00:05:43,634 --> 00:05:43,895
R.

109
00:05:43,895 --> 00:05:47,030
Ambedkar over separate electorates.

110
00:05:47,030 --> 00:05:51,819
And the Act of 1935 gave the provinces some self-rule.

111
00:05:54,469 --> 00:05:58,481
Meanwhile, the idea of separate nations was growing.

112
00:05:58,481 --> 00:06:02,190
In 1940, the Muslim League under Jinnah demanded

113
00:06:02,190 --> 00:06:04,687
separate Muslim-majority states.

114
00:06:05,437 --> 00:06:08,719
India was dragged into World War Two without being

115
00:06:08,719 --> 00:06:09,170
asked.

116
00:06:09,170 --> 00:06:12,452
Over two and a half million Indian soldiers fought

117
00:06:12,452 --> 00:06:13,288
for Britain.

118
00:06:14,038 --> 00:06:17,803
In August 1942, Gandhi gave the call: Quit India!

119
00:06:17,803 --> 00:06:18,631
Do or die!

120
00:06:18,631 --> 00:06:22,321
The leaders were arrested, but the whole country

121
00:06:22,321 --> 00:06:22,998
rose up.

122
00:06:23,748 --> 00:06:28,103
Abroad, Subhas Chandra Bose led the Indian National

123
00:06:28,103 --> 00:06:32,206
Army, and proclaimed the Azad Hind government in

124
00:06:32,206 --> 00:06:32,708
1943.

125
00:06:33,458 --> 00:06:37,645
In 1946, sailors of the Royal Indian Navy mutinied.

126
00:06:37,645 --> 00:06:41,751
Britain, exhausted by war, knew it could no longer

127
00:06:41,751 --> 00:06:42,717
hold India.

128
00:06:45,367 --> 00:06:48,297
But Hindu Muslim tensions exploded.

129
00:06:48,297 --> 00:06:52,529
Jinnah's Direct Action Day, in August 1946, brought

130
00:06:52,529 --> 00:06:55,052
terrible violence to Calcutta.

131
00:06:55,802 --> 00:06:59,668
At midnight on the fifteenth of August 1947, India

132
00:06:59,668 --> 00:07:01,032
awoke to freedom.

133
00:07:01,032 --> 00:07:04,746
But it was also divided into India and Pakistan.

134
00:07:04,746 --> 00:07:08,005
Millions were forced to leave their homes.

135
00:07:08,755 --> 00:07:12,344
Sardar Vallabhbhai Patel then united more than five

136
00:07:12,344 --> 00:07:15,795
hundred and sixty princely states into one India.

137
00:07:16,545 --> 00:07:19,900
Freedom was not won by one person, or one method.

138
00:07:19,900 --> 00:07:23,590
Moderates, Nationalists, revolutionaries, satyagrahis,

139
00:07:23,590 --> 00:07:26,475
soldiers, and millions of ordinary people.

140
00:07:26,475 --> 00:07:28,555
Together, they made it happen.

141
00:07:30,105 --> 00:07:31,803
Quick recap.

142
00:07:31,803 --> 00:07:34,415
1857, the Uprising.

143
00:07:34,415 --> 00:07:37,027
1885, the Congress.

144
00:07:37,027 --> 00:07:40,031
1905, Bengal is split.

145
00:07:40,031 --> 00:07:43,166
1919, Jallianwala Bagh.

146
00:07:43,166 --> 00:07:46,039
1930, the Salt March.

147
00:07:46,039 --> 00:07:48,390
1942, Quit India.

148
00:07:48,390 --> 00:07:51,524
And 1947, Independence.

149
00:07:53,074 --> 00:07:55,729
Which freedom fighter inspires you the most?

150
00:07:55,729 --> 00:07:58,560
Tell us in the comments, and subscribe for more

151
00:07:58,560 --> 00:07:59,858
chapters made simple.
